# Build context exclusions for deploy/Dockerfile.build.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context's own
# .dockerignore, which is why this sits beside the Dockerfile rather than in
# apps/web.
#
# The first two entries are not an optimisation, they are correctness:
#
#   node_modules  The Mac's tree is darwin/arm64. `COPY . .` lands AFTER
#                 `npm ci`, so without this line the host's darwin binaries
#                 overwrite the container's linux-x64 ones and the build dies on
#                 `Cannot find module '../lightningcss.linux-x64-gnu.node'`.
#
#   .env*         Next reads .env.local automatically. Leaving it in the context
#                 means a production bundle silently inlines
#                 NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080 and the deployed
#                 site calls the developer's laptop. Every value the build needs
#                 arrives as an explicit --build-arg instead.
node_modules
.env
.env.*

# Stale build output; the container produces its own.
.next
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
